  "note": "Annual election of one third (five seats), Friday 15 January 1909, for the places of H. G. MacGeagh, J.P., John Mahaffy, Daniel Drennan, Wm. Waite and George Turkington. Nine were nominated; two withdrew and seven went to the poll (four retiring members and Peter Breen, Joseph Herbert and Joshua McNeice). \"Out of a total of 2296 on the register some 1559 exercised the franchise\", 462 of them in the last hour; \"There were ten spoiled papers.\" The Irish News marks Breen \"(N.)\" (Nationalist); the other candidates carry no labels. The Lurgan Mail of 20 January 1912 (p. 5) gives the 1909 poll as 1,539."
